## `header` ##

<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css" type="text/css">

<div class="col50p terminal example">

...
&lt;header>
   &lt;h1>Título &lt;/h1>
   &lt;p>Informação adicional&lt;/p>
   &lt;img src="logo.png">
&lt;/header>
...

</div>
<div class=col50p >
<div class="page cozy">
    <div class="box popout" style="background: hsl(39,100%,30%)">  &lt;header&gt;   </div>
	<div class=box style="background: hsl(39,100%,30%);">  &lt;nav&gt;   </div>
	<div style="display: flex; style="background: hsl(39,100%,40%);">
		<div class=box style="flex:3; background: hsl(39,100%,50%);"> &lt;main&gt;
			<div class="box" style="background: hsl(39,100%,70%)"> &lt;article&gt;
				<div class="box" style="background: hsl(39,100%,70%)"> &lt;section&gt;</div>
			    <div class="box" style="background: hsl(39,100%,70%)"> &lt;section&gt;</div>
			</div>
			<div class=box style="background: hsl(39,100%,60%)">  &lt;footer&gt; </div>
		</div>
		<div class=box style="flex:1; background: hsl(39,100%,50%)"> &lt;aside&gt; </div>
	</div>
	<div class=box  style="background: hsl(39,100%,30%)"> &lt;footer&gt; </div>
</div>

</div>

* Identifica um bloco com cabeçalhos
* Pode conter títulos, imagens, *links* <span class=litle>(ex: `<h1>`, `<img>`, `<a>) </span> 
* Podem existir vários numa mesma página <span class=litle>(ex: `<article>`, `<section>`, etc) </span> 
* Mas não é válido em certos elementos <span class=litle>(ex: `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<address>` ) </span>


